"source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702210527968916_b16330e8", "type": "Claim", "text": "An international 
market research source projects that by 2030 the humanoid robot market will 
reach about US$4.04 billion, while Level 1–3 autonomous-driving cars will reach 
about US$172.2 billion and drones about US$163.6 billion, for a combined 
projected market size around US$339.84 billion, suggesting that humanoid robots 
will be a smaller but growing segment relative to other embodied automation 
domains.", "source_ids": ["20260702205532060585_79b003ca"], "citations": [6], 
"sources": [{"source_id": "20260702205532060585_79b003ca", "title": "[PDF] 
具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", 
"source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702210528044285_b837a935", "type": "Claim", "text": "A survey and 
accompanying figures classify control in embodied intelligence systems into 
hierarchical levels—from demand-level through task-level and planning-level down
to action-level—and present multiple example architectures of embodied AI 
systems, indicating that one mainstream technical route organizes perception, 
world modeling, and control via layered large-model involvement across these 
control hierarchies.", "source_ids": ["20260702205532099715_cc21568c", 
"20260702205532144879_6905e212"], "citations": [7, 8], "sources": [{"source_id":
"20260702205532099715_cc21568c", "title": "《数字化领航》AI应用专刊", "url": 
"https://www.h3c.com/cn/d_202604/2832716_233453_0.htm", "source_type": 
"official", "published_at": null}, {"source_id": 
"20260702205532144879_6905e212", "title": "基于大模型的具身智能系统综述 - 
自动化学报", "url": 
"https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", 
"source_type": "paper", "published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": 
"20260702210528206224_643aeb21", "type": "Claim", "text": "One analysis 
highlights the synergy among multimodal large models (MM-LLMs), world models, 
and embodied AI as a core technical route toward AGI, arguing that MM-LLMs solve
single-modality perception limits by fusing text, images, and speech, world 
models provide predictive internal representations of environment dynamics, and 
embodied AI closes the loop by executing perception–decision–action in the 
physical world, jointly shifting AI from single to multi-dimensional perception 
and from passive cognition to active prediction.", "source_ids": 
["20260702205532099715_cc21568c"], "citations": [7], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260702205532099715_cc21568c", "title": "《数字化领航》AI应用专刊", "url": 
"https://www.h3c.com/cn/d_202604/2832716_233453_0.htm", "source_type": 
"official", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": "20260702210528311345_3b23caf0", 
"type": "Claim", "text": "A generalist AI GEN-0 study cited in a Chinese 
embodied-intelligence analysis suggests an approximate scaling law in which a 
tenfold increase in training data volume yields a roughly proportional 
performance improvement of the model, and this scaling intuition is used to 
motivate large real-world data acquisition loops in embodied AI development.", 
"source_ids": ["20260702205532060585_79b003ca"], "citations": [6], "sources": 
[{"source_id": "20260702205532060585_79b003ca", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告
