"20260702210528967297_f072fb7f", "type": "Claim", "text": "Agility Robotics 
represents a practical deployment route for embodied AI in logistics: founded in
2015, it introduced the bipedal Cassie in 2017 and the more human-like Digit in 
2020, with Digit able to perform material-handling tasks in warehouses and 
outdoors and being piloted from late 2023 in Amazon fulfillment centers, marking
one of the first notable commercial deployments of humanoid robots in 
logistics.", "source_ids": ["20260702205420629658_38452154"], "citations": [5], 
"sources": [{"source_id": "20260702205420629658_38452154", "title": "21 top 
companies in the vanguard of the rise of humanoid robots", "url": 
"https://rossdawson.com/futurist/companies-creating-future/top-companies-rise-hu
manoid-robots", "source_type": "blog", "published_at": "2025-07-14"}]}, {"id": 
"20260702210529072126_1cebdc1c", "type": "Claim", "text": "Figure AI exemplifies
a high-capital, large-model-driven humanoid route targeting labor-intensive 
industrial tasks: founded in 2022 in Sunnyvale, it produced prototype Figure 01 
within a year and Figure 02 with claimed human-level hand dexterity in 2024, 
raised about US$70 million Series A in mid-2023 and US$524–675 million Series B 
in February 2024 at an approximate valuation of US$2.6 billion, and signed a 
multiyear agreement with BMW to deploy robots for material-handling tasks at the
Spartanburg plant while planning a more capable Figure 03 platform for around 
2026.", "source_ids": ["20260702205420629658_38452154", 
"20260702205532060585_79b003ca"], "citations": [5, 6], "sources": [{"source_id":
"20260702205420629658_38452154", "title": "21 top companies in the vanguard of 
