"“具身智能有别于传统 AI 线性的“输入数据－输出答案”模式， 
需要在物理环境的交互中形成自主进化的智能闭环： 本体被部署到真 
实场景中→在执行任务中收集真实行为数据→高质量数据被用于模 
型训练和迭代→更通用的模型被部署到更多的机器人上， 从而收集更 
多、更高质量的数据。”", "source_ids": ["20260702205532060585_79b003ca"], 
"citations": [6], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702205532060585_79b003ca", 
"title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", 
"source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702205537696118_434533a7", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"英文摘要写道：“Thanks to the rapid development of large-scale pre-training 
models possessing world knowledge in recent years, embodied intelligence based 
on large models has achieved good results in various tasks, demonstrating strong
generalization capabilities and broad application prospects across various 
fields. This article reviews the work of embodied intelligence based on large 
models. First, it introduces the roles of large models in perception and 
understanding within embodied intelligence systems. Second, it provides a 
relatively comprehensive summary of the four levels of control that large models
participate in within embodied intelligence: Demand-level, task-level, 
planning-level, and action-level. Subsequently, it introduces different embodied
intelligence system architectures and summarizes the current data sources for 
embodied intelligence models, including simulators, imitation learning, and 
video learning. Finally, it discusses and summarizes the challenges and 
development directions faced by embodied intelligence systems based on large 
language models (LLMs).”", "source_ids": ["20260702205532144879_6905e212"], 
"citations": [8], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702205532144879_6905e212", 
"title": "基于大模型的具身智能系统综述 - 自动化学报", "url": 
"https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", 
"source_type": "paper", "published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": 
"20260702210527068679_27e493cf", "type": "Claim", "text": "A 2025 survey article
titled \"Embodied intelligence systems based on large models: A survey\" (Acta 
Automatica Sinica, Vol. 51(1), pp. 1–19, DOI 10.16383/j.aas.c240542) provides a 
structured global overview of embodied intelligence based on large models, 
including the roles of large models in perception and understanding, a 
four-level control hierarchy (demand, task, planning, action), examples of 
system architectures, and a summary of major data sources (simulators, imitation
learning, video learning) for embodied AI models.", "source_ids": 
["20260702205532144879_6905e212"], "citations": [8], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260702205532144879_6905e212", "title": "基于大模型的具身智能系统综述 - 
自动化学报", "url": 
"https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", 
"source_type": "paper", "published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": 
"20260702210527328198_37e9bc46", "type": "Claim", "text": "According to ITU-T 
F.748.6, embodied artificial intelligence is defined as AI fused with a physical
entity that can autonomously interact with the physical world and adapt to its 
environment; based on this framework, one report summarizes that, relative to 
traditional AI systems, embodied intelligence adds three core capability 
dimensions: cognition (from seeing to understanding), collaboration (from 
single-machine execution to multi-agent cooperation), and learning (from 
learning before acting to learning during acting).", "source_ids": 
["20260702205532060585_79b003ca"], "citations": [6], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260702205532060585_79b003ca", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 
中国信息通信研究院", "url": 
"http://www.caict.ac.cn/kxyj/qwfb/bps/202601/P020260130541978285206.pdf", 
"source_type": "report", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": 
"20260702210527434444_a868ae1c", "type": "Claim", "text": "A 2025 survey and 
related analysis identify the main data sources for contemporary embodied AI and
large-model-based embodied intelligence as three categories: simulator-generated
interaction data, imitation learning from human demonstrations, and video 
learning from passive visual corpora, illustrated by the RT-X dataset as an 
example of diverse embodied data.", "source_ids": ["20260702205532144879_6905e
   1.4  212"], "citations": [8], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260702205532144879_6905e212", "title": "基于大模型的具身智能系统综述 - 
自动化学报", "url": 
"https://www.aas.net.cn/cn/article/doi/10.16383/j.aas.c240542?viewType=HTML", 
"source_type": "paper", "published_at": "2025-01-16"}]}, {"id": 
"20260702210527542149_27e419f6", "type": "Claim", "text": "One Chinese policy 
and industry analysis describes embodied intelligence as departing from linear 
\"input–output\" traditional AI by operating a 
deployment–data–training–redeployment closed loop in real physical environments:
robots are deployed into real scenes, collect task-execution behavior data, use 
high-quality data to train and iterate models, and redeploy improved general 
models to more robots to collect more and better data.", "source_ids": 
["20260702205532060585_79b003ca"], "citations": [6], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260702205532060585_79b003ca", "title": "[PDF] 具身智能发展报告 - 
